# Component Architecture — ARTSA Frontend

Sources: [nextjs-react-typescript](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules), [typescript-shadcn-ui-nextjs](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)

## Directory layout
```
frontend/
  app/              # routes only — thin page shells
  components/
    ui/             # shadcn primitives (Button, Card, …)
    layout/         # Sidebar, TopNav, PageHeader
    shared/         # SeverityBadge, RiskScore, charts
    <feature>/      # feature-specific (topology, wargame)
  lib/              # api.ts, types.ts, utils.ts, hooks/
```

## Page vs component
- Pages: wire data (fetch, WebSocket), compose layout, pass props down
- Components: presentational by default; extract hooks (`useDashboardMetrics`, `useTelemetryFeed`) when logic repeats
- Max ~150 lines per page file; split panels into named components

## Reuse patterns
- `PageHeader` — title, description, actions slot
- `StatCard` — metric tiles for command center
- `DashboardCard` — titled panel with optional badge/footer
- `EmptyState` — consistent zero-data UX across Observatory, Topology, Reports

## Data flow
- API calls through `fetchFromBackend()` only; centralize URLs in `lib/api.ts`
- WebSocket URL derived from `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` — single source of truth
- Types in `lib/types.ts` mirror backend models; don't duplicate inline `any`

## Exports
- Named exports for components; default export only for Next.js `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx`
- File name matches primary export (`SeverityBadge.tsx` → `SeverityBadge`)
